# Fidelity Ladder — instance configuration (12-factor).
# The code holds mechanisms; YOUR instance is entirely these variables. Copy to your deploy
# host's EnvironmentFile (see deploy.example/fls-harness.service) — never commit real values.

# ── the surface (GitHub App — OPTIONAL) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave this whole section unset and the ladder runs in LOCAL-MODE: `sources.kind=local`,
# `auth.kind=none` (see `GET /system` -> `app: false`). Expeditions live in the local
# ExpeditionStore, admission/climb/kill/wall all work — you just skip the GitHub App
# onboarding (docs/getting-started.md §3 becomes optional). This is the fresh-install default.
#
# To wire the real GitHub surface instead, set all three of these (auto-detected — no extra
# flag needed) and follow docs/getting-started.md §3:
# The repo whose issues ARE your expeditions. Outbound calls refuse when unset (fail-closed).
FLS_REPO=your-org/your-repo
# HMAC secret shared with your GitHub App's webhook. Unsigned/unconfigured -> 403, always.
FLS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Outbound token (App installation token or a fine-grained PAT: Issues RW + Deployments RW).
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Explicit overrides (rarely needed — auto-detect from the above is usually right):
# FLS_SOURCE_KIND=github   # or `local`
# FLS_AUTH_KIND=github-app # or `none`

# ── the adjudicator (judges) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any OpenAI-compatible Azure deployment works; unset -> admission fails closed (needs-human).
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=
AZURE_OPENAI_KEY=

# ── builders ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Metered lane (ANCHOR builder.backend: api, or the authorized fallback):
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Subscription lane (ANCHOR builder.backend: skill-server) — any server speaking
# POST {FLS_SKILL_SERVER}/invoke/{skill} with Bearer auth and {skill, output} replies:
FLS_SKILL_SERVER=
FLS_SKILL_SERVER_KEY=

# ── optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A directory containing a playwright npm install, for real rung-3 walkthroughs.
# Unset -> the walkthrough reports unavailable (fail-closed, never a fake pass).
FLS_PLAYWRIGHT_DIR=

# Admin UI build-time override (defaults to same-origin /api — see deploy.example/Caddyfile):
# VITE_FLS_API=

# Local dev tip: bridge your secret store into env with an UNTRACKED script, e.g.
#   scripts/local-env.sh   ->   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="$(your-secret-store get ...)"
# The code never reads a credential store directly.
